# /etc/udev/rules.d/70-uinput-solaar.rules — installed by chezmoi
# (system/linux/etc/**, .chezmoiscripts/30-linux/install-system-10-files).
#
# Grant the ACTIVE SEAT USER write access to /dev/uinput. Two managed
# consumers share this single grant:
#
#   - Solaar's rule engine, which synthesizes input under Wayland: the MX
#     Master gesture rules in ~/.config/solaar/rules.yaml use KeyPress
#     (Super+Left/Right window tiling on GNOME) and MouseScroll (thumb-wheel
#     horizontal scroll), and under Wayland both write through evdev uinput
#     — "For uinput to work the user must have write access for /dev/uinput"
#     (logitech_receiver/diversion.py).
#   - ydotoold, the managed ~/.config/systemd/user/ydotool.service daemon
#     (started through the ~/.local/libexec/ydotoold-active-seat wrapper),
#     which needs the same write access to inject keyboard and pointer
#     input for the active desktop user.
#
# Stock Ubuntu/Fedora grant no user access to the node. TAG+="uaccess" has
# systemd-logind maintain a per-session ACL for the active seat user —
# granted on login, revoked on seat change — instead of a permanent
# group/mode widening. This is the ONLY positive /dev/uinput grant in this
# repository; see the neighboring 80-uinput.rules for why Ubuntu's own
# broader vendor rule does not add a second one.
#
# ORDERING: the filename number MUST stay < 73 — the uaccess tag is
# processed by systemd's /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/73-seat-late.rules, and a tag
# added by a later-sorting rule is never seen. OPTIONS+="static_node=uinput"
# makes udevd apply this rule to the static /dev/uinput node at daemon
# startup, before any device event / module load.
#
# NOTE: the installer only reloads the rules database (`udevadm control
# --reload`, deliberately no `udevadm trigger`), so on the FIRST install the
# ACL lands at next boot. To grant it to the current session immediately:
#   sudo setfacl -m "u:${USER}:rw" /dev/uinput
# (the same command diversion.py's own header documents).
KERNEL=="uinput", SUBSYSTEM=="misc", OPTIONS+="static_node=uinput", TAG+="uaccess"
